{
  "summary": "The primary user flow works and passes automated accessibility (axe 0 issues, Lighthouse 98 % A11y) and layout checks. All main screens appear in the flow, the theming system is wired up and interactive components generally follow the spec. However the implementation is missing several secondary UI states and interaction details required by DESIGN.md: loading and error views for Dashboard, Receipts, Mileage and Settings are not present; focus‑visible styling for buttons is omitted; a few components still use hard‑coded colour values instead of the design tokens; the backup‑passphrase inputs lack a show/hide toggle; numeric fields do not enforce the max‑length truncation defined in the spec; the offline‑only message isn’t rendered on the Export screen; and the BottomTabBar does not expose direct shortcuts to Export, Backup and Restore as the spec states. These gaps are medium‑severity usability / accessibility gaps that should be resolved before the product is considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Dashboard screen never renders the loading `ActivityIndicator` state defined in DESIGN.md; it jumps straight to empty or populated view.",
      "fix": "Add a loading state (e.g., `isLoading` flag) that shows a centered `ActivityIndicator` while the store data is being read. Follow the spec: no copy text needed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "There is no error view with the required \"Retry\" button for data‑load failures on the Dashboard.",
      "fix": "Wrap the data‑fetch in a try/catch, set an `error` state and render a full‑screen error view containing the copy \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" and a PrimaryButton labeled \"Retry\" that re‑executes the load."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading and error states required for the Receipts screen are missing; only the list view is implemented.",
      "fix": "Introduce `Loading`, `Empty`, `Loaded` and `Error` UI variants matching the spec. Display an `ActivityIndicator` while fetching receipts and an error view with the copy \"Could not fetch receipts. Pull to retry.\" plus a retry button."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage screen lacks the loading spinner and error view defined in the design table.",
      "fix": "Add the same state handling as `ReceiptsScreen` – a centered `ActivityIndicator` for loading and a full‑screen error view with the copy \"Could not fetch mileage. Pull to retry.\" and a retry button."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings screen does not display the error `Snackbar` (\"Unable to load settings.\") when the async settings load fails.",
      "fix": "Catch errors when reading the stored settings and dispatch a `Snackbar` with the prescribed error message."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Hard‑coded colour values (e.g., \"#49454F\") are used for text and backgrounds instead of the theme tokens, risking visual inconsistency and contrast issues.",
      "fix": "Replace literal colours with values from `useTheme().colors` (e.g., `theme.colors.onSurface`, `theme.colors.surface`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus outline on web; the `:focus-visible` style required for WCAG 2.1 is not applied.",
      "fix": "Add a `focusVisibleStyle` (or CSS `:focus-visible` rule) that draws a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` when the button receives keyboard focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase fields are always masked with no eye‑icon toggle to show/hide the text, contrary to password‑field best practices.",
      "fix": "Add a trailing icon button that toggles `secureTextEntry` on the `TextInput`. Provide accessible labels \"Show passphrase\" / \"Hide passphrase\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric inputs (amount, miles, rates) accept unlimited characters; the spec requires truncation to the max allowed length and overflow to trigger the same validation error.",
      "fix": "Set appropriate `maxLength` props (e.g., 9 for amount, 5 for miles) and extend the validation logic to flag overflow. Show a `HelperText type=\"error\"` when the limit is exceeded."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When the device is offline the Export screen does not display the fullscreen \"You are offline…\" message required for any screen that may need a network call.",
      "fix": "Detect offline status via `NetInfo` and render the full‑screen offline view with the exact copy when `!isConnected`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "BottomTabBar only contains Home, Receipts, Mileage and Settings tabs; the primary actions Export, Backup and Restore are reachable only via Settings, not directly from the bar as required by the spec's \"accessible via bottom tab bar or Settings\" rule.",
      "fix": "Add three additional tabs (Export, Backup, Restore) with proper icons and labels, ensuring they are styled using the design tokens and reachable from any screen."
    }
  ]
}

