{
  "summary": "The UI implements the primary user flow and passes automated aXe checks (no violations) and scores high on accessibility (98) and best‑practices (100). All screens listed in DESIGN.md are present and the navigation flow covers every step from policy gate to delete‑all‑data. However several secondary states, token usage, and accessibility details are missing or only partially implemented. The most common gaps are: missing offline banner UI, inconsistent use of design tokens in custom components, lack of focus‑visible outlines on web, incomplete accessibility labeling for icon‑only FABs and dialogs, and a few copy mismatches in Snackbars. None of these break the core flow (no high‑severity items), but they lower the polish and could affect users with assistive technology.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "No offline‑only banner is displayed when the device is offline, even though the spec requires a full‑screen message \"You are offline…\" for any screen that may trigger a network share.",
      "fix": "Use NetInfo (or expo-network) to detect offline state and render a full‑screen view with the prescribed copy. Hide the export buttons while offline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner missing for the backup flow (network‑free but share sheet may need connectivity).",
      "fix": "Add the same offline full‑screen overlay as in ExportScreen, showing the spec copy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline UI not present for the restore flow; spec expects a full‑screen offline message where a network request would be made (share on web).",
      "fix": "Render the offline view when NetInfo reports no connection."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error state UI (full‑screen view with \"Retry\" button) is not implemented; only loading and populated states are present.",
      "fix": "Add an error component that matches the design table, showing the exact copy and a retry button that re‑fetches data."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings error state (Snackbar with \"Unable to load settings.\") is not wired; the screen only shows default content.",
      "fix": "Wrap the settings fetch in try/catch and display a Snackbar with the exact copy on failure."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "On web the button has a ripple but no visible focus outline, violating WCAG focus‑visible requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style that draws a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` (or the CSS custom property `--color-outline`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/TextButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing focus‑visible outline on web for text buttons.",
      "fix": "Apply the same `:focus-visible` outline as PrimaryButton."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The main FAB icon (plus) and the two mini‑FABs have no `accessibilityLabel`, making them invisible to screen readers.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` to the receipt mini‑FAB and `accessibilityLabel=\"Add mileage\"` to the mileage mini‑FAB (and a label for the main FAB as well)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Dialog.tsx",
      "issue": "Dialog does not trap focus and action buttons lack a focus‑visible style; keyboard users cannot navigate safely.",
      "fix": "Use `react-native-paper`'s `Dialog` with `Portal` and set `focusTrap={true}` (or manage focus manually). Add a focus outline to the Cancel/Delete buttons."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Passphrase TextInput fields are missing `secureTextEntry`, `autoComplete=\"off\"`, and a show/hide toggle, which is required for privacy and usability.",
      "fix": "Add `secureTextEntry={true}`, `autoComplete=\"off\"`, and a trailing eye‑icon button that toggles visibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase input lacks `secureTextEntry` and a visibility toggle; also missing `autoComplete=\"off\"`.",
      "fix": "Apply the same secure input pattern as in the backup passphrase screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Spacing values (margin, padding) are hard‑coded (e.g., `margin: 16`) instead of using the theme’s spacing token (`theme.spacing`).",
      "fix": "Replace all raw numeric spacings with `theme.spacing * <multiplier>` to keep the 8 dp grid consistent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Card.tsx",
      "issue": "Card border radius and elevation are hard‑coded rather than sourced from `theme.roundness` and `theme.elevation`. This deviates from the design token spec.",
