{
  "summary": "The screen works but reads as an unstyled form: the page title duplicates the app bar, every field shows a static placeholder instead of a floating Material label, an error is displayed before the user has typed anything, and the vertical rhythm between fields is uneven. Fixing the shared TextInput/FormField wrapper, the validation timing and the sticky save footer would lift this screen and every other form (mileage, backup, restore) at once.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Page heading \"Add receipt\" below the Appbar",
      "issue": "The title is duplicated — Appbar.Header already shows \"Add receipt\", so the 32px H1 wastes ~96px of the first screenful and pushes the Save button below the fold.",
      "fix": "Delete the in-page <Text variant=\"headlineMedium\">Add receipt</Text>. Keep only <Appbar.Header mode=\"small\"><Appbar.BackAction/><Appbar.Content title=\"Add receipt\"/></Appbar.Header> and start the form at paddingTop: 16. Apply the same rule in the shared screen scaffold: screens with an Appbar title never repeat it in the body.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Amount field error state on an untouched form",
      "issue": "\"Amount must be > 0\" and the red outline are shown before the user has entered anything, which reads as a failure on arrival and makes the whole form feel broken.",
      "fix": "Only pass error={touched.amount && !!errors.amount} to the Paper TextInput. Track touched on onBlur (or first change) in the shared FormField component; the Save button stays disabled for untouched invalid forms, so no error styling is needed up front.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "All text inputs (Amount, Date, Category, Notes)",
      "issue": "Field names sit inside the box as static placeholders at the same size as input text, so once a value is typed the user loses the label; the boxes also look like empty containers rather than MD3 text fields.",
      "fix": "In src/components/ui/FormField.tsx render <TextInput mode=\"outlined\" label=\"Amount\" dense={false} /> so the label floats to the notch on focus/fill. Give Amount keyboardType=\"decimal-pad\" and left={<TextInput.Affix text=\"$\" />}; give Date right={<TextInput.Icon icon=\"calendar\" />} and make it open a date picker; give Notes multiline numberOfLines={3}.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Vertical spacing between form fields",
      "issue": "Gaps are inconsistent (≈56px Amount→Date after the error, ≈72px Date→Category, ≈32px Type→Notes), so the form has no rhythm and looks hand-placed.",
      "fix": "Wrap fields in a <View style={{gap: 16}}> container with horizontal padding 24, and let FormField always reserve one line of helper space via <HelperText type=\"error\" visible={!!error} padding=\"none\"> so the layout does not shift when an error appears. No per-field margins anywhere else.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "\"Save receipt\" primary button",
      "issue": "It sits at the end of a scrolling column as a flat grey pill with low-contrast disabled text, and on phone it is near the fold; the primary action is easy to miss.",
      "fix": "Move it into a sticky footer: a Surface with elevation={2}, padding 16 plus bottom safe-area inset, holding <Button mode=\"contained\" style={{borderRadius: 12}} contentStyle={{height: 48}} labelVariant=\"labelLarge\" disabled={!isValid}>Save receipt</Button>. Extract as src/components/ui/FormFooter.tsx and reuse on the mileage form.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "\"Type\" group label and segmented control",
      "issue": "The label is teal (primary) and tiny, so it reads like a link rather than a field label, and the segments are a custom two-box control inconsistent with the rest of the form.",
      "fix": "Render the label as <Text variant=\"labelLarge\" style={{color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant, marginBottom: 8}}>Type</Text> and replace the custom control with Paper <SegmentedButtons value={type} onValueChange={setType} buttons={[{value:'expense',label:'Expense',icon:'arrow-down'},{value:'income',label:'Income',icon:'arrow-up'}]} /> so the selected state uses secondaryContainer and a check icon from the theme.",
      "shared": false
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The form reads as a stack of generic outlined boxes: the screen title is duplicated under the app bar, an error is shown on a field the user has not touched yet, vertical rhythm between fields is random (24–56px), and the inputs give no affordance for what they do (currency, date picker, category picker, photo capture). The biggest wins are a shared FormField/FormScreen pattern that fixes spacing, helper-text reservation and touched-based validation, plus concrete affordances on each control.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Screen heading \"Add receipt\" (below the Appbar)",
      "issue": "The title is rendered twice — in the Appbar.Header and again as a large headline — wasting ~88px of the first screenful and making the hierarchy ambiguous.",
      "fix": "Delete the in-body <Text variant=\"headlineMedium\">Add receipt</Text>. Keep only Appbar.Header + Appbar.BackAction + Appbar.Content title=\"Add receipt\" (titleLarge). Start the scroll content at 24px top padding so the first control is the photo action.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Amount field error state",
      "issue": "\"Amount must be > 0\" is shown in red with a red outline on first render, before the user has typed anything; the form greets the user with a failure and a disabled Save.",
      "fix": "In the shared FormField, track `touched` and only pass `error={touched && !!errorText}`; show HelperText type=\"error\" only when touched. Until then render HelperText type=\"info\" with the hint (e.g. \"Required\") so the field keeps the same height.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Vertical spacing between form fields",
      "issue": "Gaps are inconsistent (24px after photo, 48px after the error, 56px before Category, 40px before Save) because HelperText space is not reserved, so each field shifts the rhythm.",
      "fix": "Create src/components/ui/FormField.tsx that wraps TextInput (mode=\"outlined\") + HelperText with a fixed container marginBottom: 16 and HelperText style={{minHeight: 20}} rendered always (visible={true}, empty string when valid). Remove all ad-hoc margins from the screen; the ScrollView uses contentContainerStyle={{padding: 16, paddingBottom: 24}}.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Amount / Date / Category inputs",
      "issue": "All three are identical empty outlined boxes with no affordance: no currency symbol, no numeric keyboard, no calendar or dropdown indicator, so the user cannot tell Date and Category open pickers.",
      "fix": "Amount: <TextInput label=\"Amount\" keyboardType=\"decimal-pad\" left={<TextInput.Affix text=\"$\" />} />. Date: render as a pressable field with right={<TextInput.Icon icon=\"calendar\" />} and editable={false} opening the date picker. Category: right={<TextInput.Icon icon=\"menu-down\" />} opening a Paper Menu of categories. Keep all three at the default 56px outlined height.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "\"Add photo\" button",
      "issue": "A full-width text-only outlined button in primary blue reads like another empty input and gives no sense of the resulting attachment.",
      "fix": "Replace with <Button mode=\"outlined\" icon=\"camera\" onPress={pickPhoto} contentStyle={{height: 48}} style={{borderRadius: 12, marginBottom: 24}}>Add photo</Button>. After a photo is chosen, swap it for a 96x96 Image in a Card with a Chip/IconButton icon=\"close\" to remove, left-aligned above the fields.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "\"Type\" label + segmented control",
      "issue": "The label is teal primary-coloured body text that competes with the inputs, and the two-button group is a custom control that does not match Paper's field styling.",
      "fix": "Use <Text variant=\"labelLarge\" style={{color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant, marginBottom: 8}}>Type</Text> and Paper's <SegmentedButtons value={type} onValueChange={setType} density=\"regular\" buttons={[{value:'expense', label:'Expense', icon:'arrow-down'}, {value:'income', label:'Income', icon:'arrow-up'}]} /> with 24px marginBottom, so the selected state uses theme secondaryContainer/onSecondaryContainer.",
      "shared": false
    }
  ]
}

